 baby: a dynamic model of reproductive decision-making and evidence from Gabbra pastoralists</article-title><source>Ethol. Sociobiol</source><volume>17</volume><year>1996</year><fpage>263</fpage><lpage>273</lpage><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://dx.doi.org/doi:10.1016/0162-3095(96)00044-1">doi:10.1016/0162-3095(96)00044-1</ext-link></citation></ref><ref id="bib33"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mace</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The evolutionary ecology of human family size</article-title><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Dunbar</surname><given-names>R.I.M</given-names></name><name><surname>Barrett</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><source>The Oxford handbook of evolutionary psychology</source><year>2007</year><publisher-name>Oxford University Press</publisher-name><publisher-loc>Oxford, UK</publisher-loc><fpage>383</fpage><lpage>396</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="bib34"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Moring</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Household and family in Finnish Coastal Societies 1635&#x02013;1895</article-title><source>J. Family Hist</source><volume>18</volume><year>1993</year><fpage>395</fpage><lpage>414</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="bib35"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Moring</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Motherhood, milk, and money: infant mortality in pre-industrial Finland</article-title><source>Soc. Hist. Med</source><volume>11</volume><year>1998</year><fpage>177</fpage><lpage>196</lpage><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://dx.doi.org/doi:10.1093/shm/11.2.177">doi:10.1093/shm/11.2.177</ext-link><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11620426</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib36"><c